<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Taifa of Menorca</h1><p class="st-meta">1228 CE – 1287 CE (approx.) · capital Ciutadella</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An autonomous Muslim island state that survived for half a century as a tributary of Aragon after the Christian conquest of Majorca.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-i-of-aragon">James I of Aragon</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> in 1229, the Muslim leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Menorca</a> agreed in 1231, by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-capdepera">Treaty of Capdepera</a>, to recognise him as overlord and pay tribute, while keeping their own government, law and religion. The island was known in Arabic as Manurqa.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The island was ruled by a ra'is from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciutadella-de-menorca">Madina Manurqa</a>, the later Ciutadella. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abu-uthman-said-ibn-hakam">Abu Uthman Said ibn Hakam</a> (ruled 1234-1282), a scholar and poet, gathered a library and kept the island prosperous through farming, livestock and trade with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> while paying tribute to Aragon.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In January 1287 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-aragon">Alfonso III of Aragon</a> invaded, accusing the island of aiding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hafsid-sultanate">Hafsid Sultanate</a>. Most inhabitants were enslaved or expelled, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Menorca</a> was resettled by Catalans as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-majorca">Kingdom of Majorca</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1228 CE – 1287 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:84.14%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1228 CE – 1287 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ciutadella</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Abu Uthman Said ibn Hakam, Abu Umar ibn Said</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Manurqa, Almoxarifate of Menorca</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1258&amp;focus=taifa-of-menorca" aria-label="Taifa of Menorca on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4779 748 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Taifa of Menorca lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5099 1004L4794 1282M5099 1004L4984 945"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4794 1282h0M4984 945h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5099 1004h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5099 1004h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1258&amp;focus=taifa-of-menorca">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
